---
// La pagina che Apple pretende per pubblicare un'app. Il testo viene dai
// documenti veri dei tre progetti, non da un modello generico: e' per questo
// che dice cose diverse per ciascuno dei tre motori di Minta invece di una
// riga sola buona per tutto.
//
// Le note interne, le verifiche e il ragionamento sul ruolo di titolare
// restano in PRIVACY-BOZZA.md e non si pubblicano.
//
// ATTENZIONE alla frase sullo Zero Data Retention di Groq: e' vera finche'
// quell'interruttore resta acceso nella console di Groq, e nessun test di
// questo sito puo' accorgersi se viene spento. Se tocchi le impostazioni di
// Groq, rileggi questa pagina.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const aggiornata = '9 August 2026';
---

<Base
  titolo="Privacy — TROVA.ME"
  descrizione="What each TROVA.ME app does with your data, in plain terms. On your iPhone nothing leaves the phone; with Minta Cloud nothing is kept, by anyone."
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>

  <p class="apertura">
    TROVA.ME is one person making three iPhone apps. This page says what each app does with
    your data, in plain terms. It is short because the apps collect very little.
  </p>

  <p>
    The data controller is <strong>Daniele Riccarand</strong>, acting as an individual, in
    Milan, Italy. For anything on this page, write to <a href="mailto:dan@trova.me"
      >dan@trova.me</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    This site has no analytics, no cookies, no trackers and no contact form. Nothing you do
    here is recorded. It is a set of static pages served by GitHub Pages which — like any
    web server — logs requests at its own level; TROVA.ME neither receives nor stores those
    logs.
  </p>

  <h2>Minta</h2>
  <p>
    Minta records audio, transcribes it, and rewrites the transcript. <strong
      >You choose where that work happens, and the choice decides where your words go.</strong
    >
  </p>

  <div class="motore">
    <h3>On your iPhone</h3>
    <p>
      Transcription uses Apple’s on-device speech recognition and summaries use Apple’s
      on-device models. Your audio and your text never leave the phone. This has been
      checked the plain way: in airplane mode, with this engine selected, recording,
      transcription and summarising all still work.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="motore">
    <h3>With your own API key</h3>
    <p>
      Your transcript is sent directly from your iPhone to the AI provider you chose —
      OpenAI, Anthropic or Google — under your own account and their terms. TROVA.ME is not
      part of that exchange and never sees your key, which is stored in the iPhone’s
      keychain.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="motore">
    <h3>Minta Cloud</h3>
    <p>
      Audio and transcripts are sent to <code>api.trova.me</code>, which forwards them to
      Groq, the provider that performs the transcription and the summarisation. The
      TROVA.ME server stores neither your audio nor your text: it processes the request,
      returns the result, and keeps only a ledger entry recording that credit was spent.
    </p>
    <p>
      Groq acts as a processor on TROVA.ME’s instructions, under Groq’s Data Processing
      Addendum, and <strong>Zero Data Retention is switched on for this account: Groq keeps
      nothing</strong> — not the audio, not the transcript, not the summary, not even the
      short-lived logs it would otherwise keep to troubleshoot its own platform. Groq
      operates in the United States, and the transfer is covered by the EU Standard
      Contractual Clauses included in that addendum.
    </p>
    <p>
      So, end to end: your words are processed and then they are gone. Nobody in this chain
      keeps them. The only thing that survives a Minta Cloud request is the line in the
      ledger saying that some credit was spent.
    </p>
    <p>
      To use Minta Cloud you sign in with Apple. TROVA.ME receives the identifier Apple
      issues for you — not your name, not your email — and uses it for one purpose only:
      keeping track of your credit balance. That identifier and your balance are kept for
      as long as you have credit. Purchases are handled by Apple; TROVA.ME never sees your
      payment details.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    Your recordings, transcripts and summaries are stored on your iPhone. Deleting a
    session deletes them.
  </p>

  <h2>Pronto</h2>
  <p>
    Your list lives on your iPhone. <strong>There is no Pronto account and no Pronto
    server.</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    To understand what you dictate, Pronto sends what you said — together with the tasks
    already on your list, so that “move the dentist to Thursday” has something to refer to
    — to the AI provider you chose. That exchange happens directly between your iPhone and
    the provider, with your own key, under your own account and their terms. TROVA.ME is
    not part of it and never sees the key, which is stored in the iPhone’s keychain. If you
    never configure a provider, nothing is sent anywhere.
  </p>

  <h2>ClaudePal</h2>
  <p>
    ClaudePal is an experiment and is not distributed. It connects your iPhone to a Claude
    Code session running on your own Mac, over your own local network. Nothing is sent to
    TROVA.ME. What Claude Code itself sends to Anthropic is governed by Anthropic’s terms
    and by your own account.
  </p>
  <p>
    The connection is not encrypted and is intended for a trusted network only. This is
    stated plainly on the ClaudePal page as well.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>None of these apps are directed at children.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If any of this changes, this page changes with it, and the date below changes too.
  </p>

  <p class="stato">Last updated: {aggiornata}</p>
</Base>

